# Supabase Configuration

Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in your Supabase project credentials.

```bash
cp .env.example .env.local
```

## Required Variables

```
# Public (browser-safe) — these are safe to expose
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Server-only — NEVER prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_, NEVER expose to browser
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key
```

## Notes

- The `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix makes these variables accessible in the browser.
- **Never commit `.env.local`** to version control.
- Use the **anon key** (public) in browser/client code — RLS is enforced.
- The **service-role key** bypasses RLS — use only in server-side API routes.
  - It must NEVER be prefixed with `NEXT_PUBLIC_`.
  - It must NEVER be imported in client components.
  - It must NEVER appear in the browser bundle.
